.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW-INSPECT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-inspect - Show daemon-local HTTP captures


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview inspect <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show daemon-local HTTP captures

.PP
Read or manage bounded HTTP captures retained by the local daemon for one preview. --body and --raw expose capture content, while enable, disable, and purge change capture state; treat output as potentially sensitive.

.PP
A preview exposes a local target through a temporary Paperboat URL or private/team access policy. Inspect its status before sharing the URL, and stop or delete it when no longer needed. Browser HTTP terminates TLS at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP[=false]
	capture redacted request/response bodies with --enable

.PP
\fB--cursor\fP=""
	continue after a capture cursor

.PP
\fB--disable\fP[=false]
	disable capture for this resource

.PP
\fB--enable\fP[=false]
	enable capture for this resource

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for inspect

.PP
\fB--id\fP=""
	show one capture by ID

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=20
	maximum captures per request (1-100)

.PP
\fB--purge\fP[=false]
	purge retained captures for this resource

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	retain exact raw requests for replay with --enable


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
